    "prompt": "The cards 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 are placed into two boxes. The sums of the numbers in each box are the same. Which number must be in the box that contains the number 4?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2021-g0102/q15.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "only 3"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "only 5"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "only 6"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "2 and 3"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "2 and 5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Half of the total",
        "body": "$2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 20$, so each box has sum 10.\n\nThe box with 4 needs 6 more. From the cards 2, 3, 5, 6 the only way to get 6 is the card 6 alone ($2 + 3 = 5$, $2 + 5 = 7$, $3 + 5 = 8$). So the boxes are {4, 6} and {2, 3, 5}.\n\n**Answer: (C) only 6**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Check the choices",
        "body": "- 4 + 3 = 7, 4 + 5 = 9: not 10.\n- 4 + 6 = 10 ✓\n- 4 + 2 + 3 = 9, 4 + 2 + 5 = 11: not 10.\n\n**Answer: (C) only 6**"
      }
    ],
