    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Three places for the shape",
        "body": "The 2 × 2 shape fits on the grid in only 3 places: top right, bottom left and bottom right. Each of the three square stickers is in a corner that only **one** of these places covers:\n\n- top right corner: only the top-right place,\n- bottom left corner: only the bottom-left place,\n- bottom right corner: only the bottom-right place.\n\nSo the three hidden numbers tell how many times each place was used, and their sum is the total number of times Carl placed the shape.\n\nThe middle cell with 15 is covered by **all three** places, so Carl placed the shape 15 times.\n\n**Answer: (D) 15**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Find each number",
        "body": "Call the numbers of times top-right = $a$, bottom-left = $b$, bottom-right = $c$.\n\n- Middle cell: $a + b + c = 15$.\n- Cell with 9 (right of the middle) is covered by top-right and bottom-right: $a + c = 9$, so $b = 6$.\n- Cell with 8 (below the middle) is covered by bottom-left and bottom-right: $b + c = 8$, so $c = 2$ and $a = 7$.\n\nSquares: $7 + 6 + 2 = 15$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 15**"
      }
    ],
